      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47367",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 2, & x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nI. It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\nII. It is **not** continuous at $x=1$ but it is differentiable at $x=1$\n\nIII. It is **not** differentiable on the interval $x\\in (-2,2)$"
